1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 e6 4. O-O Nge7 5. Re1 g6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 $6 7. e5 $14 Bg7 8. Nc3 Qc7 9. Ne4 $1 $16 Bxe5 $2 10. Nxe5 Qxe5 11. d4 $1 cxd4 (11... Qxd4 12. Nd6+ Kd7 13. Qf3 $1 $18) 12. Bg5 $1 $18 Qc7 13. Nf6+ Kd8 14. Qxd4+ Bd7 15. Nxd7 {"I played against A Adorjan with black in another Chess Magazine Festival. 1973 I think. Andreas slaughtered me in less than 10 moves. The press came up and asked whether it was a publishable game. I lied saying I just blundered horribly. Thus it was never published. Otherwise it would appear in anthologies. I do not have it." (Stewart Reuben, English Forum, 2017)} 1-0

