1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Bc4 Nf6 6. Nxc3 Bb4 7. e5 d5 8. exf6 dxc4 9. Qxd8+ Nxd8 10. fxg7 Rg8 11. Bh6 Bxc3+ 12. bxc3 Ne6 13. O-O-O Nxg7 14. Rhe1+ Be6 $6 (14... Ne6 $142 {Norris,A (2265)-Formanek,E (2330)/ Philips&Drew Knights 1982 (14)/1/2-1/2} 15. Nd4 Bd7 16. Nf5 Rxg2 17. Ng7+ Ke7 18. Nf5+ Kd8 $17) 15. Ng5 ({After the game Karaklaic, who had been following my games after our draw, pointed out the strength of} 15. g4 $142 $1 Rd8 ({Houdini prefers} 15... Ke7 16. Nd4 Kf6 17. Bf4 {Levy,D (2320)-MacDonald Ross,M (2280)/SCO-ch83 Dundee 1976 (3)/1-0} Rae8 18. h3 h5 $11) 16. Nd4 Rd5 17. f4 c5 18. Nf5 {Schiffer,K (2300)-Belic,J (2345)/BL2-West 9495 1994 (6.4)/1-0} Rxd1+ (18... Rxf5 19. gxf5 Nxf5 20. Bg5) 19. Kxd1 Nxf5 20. gxf5 Rg2 21. fxe6 Rxa2 22. exf7+ Kxf7 23. Bg5 {with advantage}) 15... Nf5 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Rxe6+ $2 ({White needs to leave the weak e-pawn and protect his own king's side pawns.} 17. g3 Ke7 18. Bf4 Nd6 19. Re5 $11) 17... Kf7 18. Rde1 Rxg2 $19 19. Bf4 Rxf2 20. Bg5 Rf8 21. Be7 Nxe7 ({Better is} 21... Ng7 $1 22. R6e4 Re8) 22. Rxe7+ Kf6 23. R1e6+ ({Better is} 23. Rxc7 Rf7 24. Rxc4 $15) 23... Kf5 24. Re5+ Kg6 25. h4 R8f7 {Now black's winning.} 26. R7e6+ Kg7 27. h5 Rh2 28. Rg5+ Kf8 29. Re1 Rxa2 30. Kb1 Raf2 31. Re6 a5 (31... Rf1+ 32. Kb2 R7f2+ 33. Ka3 Rb1 {forces mate e.g.} 34. h6 Rb3+ 35. Ka4 Ra2#) 32. h6 (32. Re1 {was forced to avoid mate.}) 32... Rf1+ 33. Kb2 R7f2+ 0-1

